<FEEDBACK>{"role":"prior","has_change":true,"feedback":"Prior edits to raise clustering ARI by tightening resource relevance, alignment, and graph quality: 1) Align shapes with downstream: restrict S and A to kept genes (keep_flag==True) before saving; also export the exact kept gene ordering (e.g., gene_list.txt and index_keep.npy) so preprocess/model use identical dimensions without ad hoc slicing. 2) Dataset-aware filtering of CellMarker/GO/MSigDB sets: compute per-gene detection fraction from the input AnnData (counts>0 frequency) and drop sets whose in-vocab detected gene fraction is below a threshold (e.g., ≥40–50% of members detected in ≥1–2% cells). This removes tissue-irrelevant marker/pathway noise (e.g., keratinocyte, neuro) and sharpens latent structure. 3) Ubiquity handling: compute “overly-ubiquitous” only over non-marker pathway sets to avoid banning multi-marker immune genes; prefer soft-penalizing ubiquity via an IDF term instead of hard-banning (except for MT and mapping errors). 4) Gene-set incidence weighting: incorporate gene rarity into S by multiplying each membership by IDF_j = log(1 + n_sets / (1 + gene_set_count_j)) (optionally combine with set weight 1/sqrt(size)), then row-normalize. This boosts discriminative markers and reduces influence of broad sets, improving the initialization of W_gs and the Laplacian signal. 5) Gene-gene graph sharpening: compute A_sets from an IDF-weighted binary B (as above) and calibrate the 0.7/0.3 mix with A_nest by normalizing both to equal Frobenius norm (or degree-sum) before mixing; then keep_topk and row-normalize. This prevents A_nest from being drowned or dominating arbitrarily. 6) Deduplication quality: dedupe across sources/categories too and collapse normalized names (case/punctuation-insensitive) with Jaccard>0.95; when collapsing, retain the variant with highest in-dataset coverage/detection (or prefer CellMarker > Hallmark > GO). 7) Mapping robustness: also exclude “mapped errors” using meta_info.error (non-empty/non-NaN) and drop summary_type entries that are non-protein-coding/pseudogene; log counts removed by each rule. 8) Canonicalization safety: avoid removing hyphens from symbols to keep HGNC fidelity and inter-op with external tools; only uppercase and strip version suffixes. 9) Efficiency/stability: compute Jaccard on the kept genes only; guard B^T B with chunking for large vocabularies; skip rows with degree<2 early. 10) Export QC to guide tuning: add to set_meta per-set coverage (fraction detected), mean detection of its genes, and to gene_vocab a ‘set_count’/‘marker_flag’; these enable downstream thresholding and hyperparam sweeps. 11) Paths: write/symlink artifacts to the plan’s /runsv3/priors directory so downstream always consumes the same canonical locations."}</FEEDBACK>

