- Weight prior and Laplacian penalties by prior confidence: multiply per-edge prior proximity by (set_weight × gene_prior_weight), and scale Laplacian by gene_prior_weight on both sides to trust curated edges more than weakly supported genes.
- Add an auxiliary loss to stabilize the set bottleneck: MSE(set_recon, stop_grad(set_act)) so the decoder learns to reconstruct meaningful set activities, reducing collapse and improving interpretability.
- Encourage subspace separation: add an orthogonality/decorr penalty between marker dims and the remaining latent (and optionally between latent and set_act), and a covariance off-diagonal penalty to reduce redundancy across latent dims; this improves clusterability.
- Complement MMD with a domain-adversarial head (gradient reversal) on z; alternate or jointly optimize with small weight to remove batch signal not captured by MMD, improving batch mixing without over-smoothing.
- Use dynamic loss reweighting (e.g., uncertainty weighting or GradNorm) to keep gradients from recon/prior/MMD/DEC on similar scales; log per-loss magnitudes and adapt weights to prevent any single term from dominating and hurting ARI.
- If keeping DEC, standardize z consistently before computing distances, warm-start λ_dec small and ramp it up, and refresh targets more frequently at the start of the clustering phase; also use cosine distance by L2-normalizing z before KMeans/Student-t to better match downstream clustering.
- Choose k and fit scalers on train+val only to avoid test leakage: fit StandardScaler and select k via silhouette on train+val, then apply the chosen model to all splits; this typically yields more reliable clusters and better ARI on held-out data.
- Improve clustering robustness if not switching to Leiden: run an ensemble of KMeans (different seeds) and use consensus labels; compute silhouette with cosine distance; this reduces variance in ARI.
- Make the Laplacian loss scale-invariant: use the symmetric normalized Laplacian and normalize the loss by Frobenius norm of W or trace(L) to keep gradients comparable across datasets; monitor its magnitude to tune λ_lap.
- Add a small consistency regularizer on cluster assignments: augment cells with light gene dropout/noise and enforce consistent soft assignments (q) across views; this sharpens clusters without labels.
- Tie training schedule to validation structure: include a validation silhouette term (on train+val) in the early-stopping objective (small weight) so stopping reflects cluster quality, not just reconstruction; use EMA of val objective for smoother decisions.
- Initialize encoder/decoder with Xavier (gain for ReLU) and consider AMP to increase batch size (helps MMD/DEC statistics) without changing math; keep grad clip but log gradient norms per block to catch instabilities.
