- Loads latent embedding and metadata; aligns with concatenated AnnData (train/val/test).
- Standardizes embedding on train+val (global scaler) and applies per-domain standardization (stats from train+val per domain), then builds cosine-normalized copy.
- Clustering model selection on train+val:
  - Leiden grid over n_neighbors ∈ {10,20,30,50}, metric ∈ {cosine, euclidean}, resolution ∈ [0.2,2.0] step 0.1, seeds {0,1,2}.
  - Scores each config by mean silhouette (primary) and label stability (mean pairwise ARI across seeds, tie-breaker).
  - Competes with KMeans (k from DEC k_opt ±{0..2} if available, else {4,6,8,10}) scored by silhouette (euclidean).
- Final labeling:
  - If KMeans wins: fit on train+val, predict all cells.
  - Else: run Leiden on train+val with best params and transfer labels to test by nearest centroid (cosine or euclidean to match metric).
  - Post-hoc: single-pass kNN label smoothing (k=30, threshold 0.6) and merging clusters smaller than 20 cells into nearest large cluster by centroid.
- Evaluation: ARI overall and per split (train/val/test) vs ground-truth cell_type.
