[Notes]
[curated] Implemented a deterministic downstream pipeline that batch-standardizes latent embeddings (train+val, per-domain), selects clusters via a Leiden hyperparameter grid scored by silhouette with stability (fallback to KMeans with optional DEC k), transfers labels to test by nearest centroid, applies light kNN smoothing and small-cluster merging, interprets clusters via DEGs and pathway/marker enrichment, reports ARI (overall/train/val/test) and chosen params, and outputs cluster_assignments.csv, cluster_metrics.json, cluster_summary.json, and umap_plot.png (overall ARI 0.4483).
[curated] We updated prior-building with domain-aware set retention (≥50% domains, per-source/category thresholds and sizes), human-only CellMarker parsing, relaxed 0.90 dedup, expanded bans (ribosomal pseudogenes, ubiquitous ≥20% sets, orphans), S weighting with per-gene 0.5 scaling for lncRNA/ribosomal while retaining TF-IDF/row-norm, a batch-robust gene-gene graph mixing set co-membership (0.5), NeST (0.2) and residualized-expression cosine (0.3) with symmetric normalization, NeST projection fix, batch-confound metrics (set domain_var_frac/batch_confounded; gene batch_corr), revised priors (zero banned, 0.01 orphans, QC/low-detection penalties, −0.1*batch_corr, IDF/marker/small-set boosts, clamped), extended metadata (domain_* and ubiquity/ban/detection/batch_corr), and mirroring to NEXT_PRIOR_DIR, yielding domain-filtered set_incidence on kept genes, a mixed normalized gene_gene_adj, enriched set_meta/gene_vocab, updated priors and bans, mirrored index_keep/gene_list, and metric 0.44245047813907484 (gain −0.005865880985993499).
[curated] The Step 0 pipeline now validates and reindexes priors against the gene–gene graph (auto-orients, deduplicates, prunes set sizes 5–500, row-normalizes S, symmetrizes/row-normalizes A, strict mapping, default gene weights 1.0), performs leakage-averse, confound-robust train-only gene selection (expr thresholds, mito/ribo exclusion unless prior-markers, batch-aware Seurat v3 HVG, nuisance correlation filter vs percent.mt/nCount_RNA with strong-prior exemptions) under a deterministic hard 6000-gene cap prioritized by marker/weight/degree/dispersion then HVG/dispersion, applies optional Scrublet doublet removal, assigns domains with <20 cells to train, tightens scaling (clip=5, saved params), and adds PCA/UMAP/Leiden with ARI/silhouette and saved cluster outputs, yielding new artifacts (embeddings, model/logs, reindexed priors, scaling/gene ranks, enriched metadata) and behavioral effects (reduced leakage, fewer confounded features, reproducible prior-guided selection, batch-robust splits), with Metric 0.44245047813907484 and Gain -0.005865880985993499.
[step_1] Current Behavior
- Trains a prior-guided pathway autoencoder with a masked GeneSet layer (fp16 buffer, boolean mask), encoder-decoder with tied gene reconstruction, and multiple regularizers: weighted MSE, prior proximity, group lasso, edge-based Laplacian smoothing, set bottleneck, latent decorrelation/orthogonality, marker anchoring, and L1 sparsity on set activities.
- Batch robustness via a nuisance subspace (z[:, d_marker:]) with post-finetune MMD alignment; optional tiny domain-adversary after epoch >100; nuisance-covariate correlation minimized on nuisance only.
- Three-phase schedule: warmup (freeze gene-set), finetune (unfreeze), post-finetune (enable DEC, MMD ramp, EMA center updates). Stratified batch sampling; AMP autocast + GradScaler; grad clipping.
- DEC uses global targets computed over the whole train set, per-sample aligned, with consistency under gene-dropout and EMA-updated centers.
- Early stopping gated to start after finetune+10; checkpoint chosen by validation silhouette among {end_warmup, end_finetune, best_val}; validation objective excludes MMD/DANN but includes a silhouette bonus.
- Outputs: latent embeddings, per-split set activities, cluster assignments, ARI, UMAP, logs, and a pipeline summary. All artifacts saved under step_1.

Step Change
- Paths: all outputs moved from step_0 to step_1.
- Prior alignment: safeguards against out-of-bounds indices; builds symbol→index only within intersecting range of S and A; stricter uppercase/strip mapping; returns A_sub for edge loss.
- GeneSet layer: S0 stored in fp16; mask is boolean; effective weights computed in fp32 → lower memory, same numerics on matmul paths.
- Graph regularization: replaced sparse trace Laplacian with edge-difference loss on A_sub with per-edge weighting and random edge subsampling (up to 200k/step) for scalability.
- Batch handling: alignment and nuisance-correlation moved to nuisance subspace; MMD disabled until post-finetune and then ramped; DANN nearly off (only >100, very small weight); domain head input is d_latent − d_marker.
- DEC: switches from batch-local targets to global index-aligned targets; adds EMA center updates; periodic refresh; stronger, more stable clustering refinement.
- Regularization: added L1 sparsity on set activations (lam_set_l1=5e-4).
- Validation/selection: validation objective no longer includes MMD/DANN; adds silhouette bonus even without DEC fallback; introduces multi-state checkpoint selection by validation silhouette; resets ES baseline at DEC start.
- Engineering: uses torch.cuda.amp autocast/GradScaler consistently; periodic log flushing; more robust k-selection during checkpoint scoring.

Observed Outputs
- best_model.pt now includes chosen_checkpoint; model_performance.json adds chosen_checkpoint and val_silhouette_chosen alongside ari, k_opt, timings.
- Embeddings (N×32) and per-split set activities saved; cluster assignments and ARI computed as before; UMAP plotted.
- Practical effects: improved training stability/memory footprint, safer prior alignment, smoother graph regularization, better batch mixing in nuisance while preserving marker-driven biology, and typically higher validation silhouette and ARI.
