<LM_OUTPUT> {"role":"biology","feedback":"Clustering and selection\n- Expand KMeans k search adaptively (e.g., k in 2..min(50, sqrt(n))) and try both cosine and euclidean; select by train+val silhouette (anchors), not train-only. Record stability over multiple random inits and prefer stable solutions.\n- Add an SNN/mutual-NN graph variant and run KMeans on its Laplacian eigenmap or use spectral on the SNN; this often sharpens boundaries in low-d manifolds.\n- Replace the hardcoded k_transfer=15 fallback: choose k for label propagation without labels by maximizing anchor neighbor-purity (mean fraction of same-cluster neighbors) or anchor silhouette after self-propagation; use that k to propagate to non-anchors.\n- Gate postprocessing more biologically: only merge a small cluster into a target if (i) silhouette improves or is unchanged and (ii) its top-DE set overlaps >50% with the target’s top-DE set or has <5 significant DEGs at FDR<0.05; otherwise keep it.\n\nBiological coherence and DEGs\n- Do DE on the full gene space used in the model (or HVGs ∪ all prior genes), not on a reduced HVG-only subset; this avoids dropping marker genes and inflating ribosomal/housekeeping hits.\n- Exclude non-informative genes using gene_vocab flags: filter mitochondrial, ribosomal (RPL/RPS), pseudogenes, and housekeeping from DE outputs. Enforce: min_pct_in ≥ 0.2, pct_in − pct_out ≥ 0.1, and log2FC ≥ 0.25 alongside BH-FDR<0.05; report effect sizes and pct_in/out.\n- Prefer pseudobulk DE (aggregate counts per cluster) for stability; if staying single-cell, use Wilcoxon or presto with tie correction and multiple-testing control per cluster.\n\nPathway/marker activities\n- Use the model’s set_activity_{train|val|test}.npy as the primary activity matrix for enrichment (it reflects the learned prior-guided layer). If that’s unavailable, compute activities from expression using all prior-in-vocab genes (not HVG-only), keeping the original set weights.\n- In reporting, enforce significance: only show sets with FDR<0.05 and AUC≥0.6; if none meet criteria, state “no significant sets” instead of listing q=1.0 entries. Clip extremely small q-values to a minimum (e.g., 1e-300) to avoid 0.0 in outputs.\n- For marker concordance, compare each cluster’s top DEGs against marker sets using all significant DEGs rather than the top-20 list to reduce stochasticity; report overlap size and Jaccard.\n\nMetrics and QC\n- During selection, compute and log train+val silhouette for the chosen solution; also log consensus stability (mean pairwise ARI across seeds). Keep ARI evaluation strictly post hoc using obs['cell_type'].\n- Add batch-mixing metrics (ASW-batch or iLISI) on the latent to catch domain leakage; include them in downstream JSON.\n\nImplementation nits\n- Try both cosine and euclidean variants when selecting; keep the better one by silhouette.\n- Set UMAP n_neighbors=30 to match the kNN graph scale used for clustering; use the same metric as the chosen clustering variant."} </LM_OUTPUT>

