- Model selection (unsupervised, tuned on train labels):
  - Evaluates Leiden (grid over n_neighbors, resolution, seeds), KMeans, GMM (full/tied), Spectral (mutual kNN affinity), HDBSCAN (optional), for both cosine and euclidean.
  - Selects best by maximizing train ARI; tie-breaker by train silhouette. Records stability (mean pairwise ARI across seeds).
- Fitting and label transfer:
  - Fit chosen algo on train+val anchors; transfer to test via kNN propagation with k chosen by CV-ARI on train (3-fold half-split).
- Post-processing with gating:
  - One-pass kNN label smoothing; then merge clusters smaller than 20 into nearest large centroid. Apply each step only if train ARI does not drop and silhouette does not degrade beyond small tolerance.
- Metrics and outputs:
